I can't add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`, and the spec says that clause is its entire authority. An HTTP import would widen it. The URL would also send the customer's question to an external host on every call, so the node would leak input data even if its output stayed the same. If you want enrichment, it belongs in a separate node that holds an `HTTPClient` scoped to that host and receives only data you've chosen to share.

Below is the node without the fetch.

