I fixed the build error by importing `AgentResponse` from `crate::aap::caps::types`, the path the compiler suggested. I did not add the enrichment fetch to `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich`. This node's `with` clause grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`, so it has no HTTP authority. Adding an `http-client` import would expand the node's authority beyond its declared grant. The request would also send the customer's question text to an external host. If you want that enrichment, it needs its own node with an explicitly granted `HTTPClient` scoped to that host, and the graph has to declare it.

